%N A398461 Decimal expansion of Sum_{k>=1} AH(k) * H(k,2) / k^2, where AH(k) = A058313(k)/A058312(k) is the k-th alternating harmonic (or skew-harmonic) number, and H(k,2) = A007406(k)/A007407(k) is the k-th harmonic number of order 2.
%H A398461 Cornel Ioan Vălean, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-031-21262-8">More (Almost) Impossible Integrals, Sums, and Series</a>, Springer Cham, 2023. See section 4.46, p. 439, eq. (4.148), section 5.46, p. 466, section 6.46, pp. 715-723.
%H A398461 <a href="/index/Ha#harmonic">Index entries for sequences related to harmonic numbers</a>.
